  "report_markdown": "# Cap Table \u2014 Cadence\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nModeled 2 scenario(s) for Cadence: 1 full, 0 mixed, 0 repay-only, 1 priced-round terms not set yet.\n1 counsel-review item(s) surfaced. 14 date-sensitive item(s) in watchlist.\nFounder ownership ranges 63.3% to 63.3% across resolved scenarios.\n\n> \u26a0 **Cap base was NOT produced by the deterministic spreadsheet mapper.** It was entered\n> manually or extracted from a document (PDF / Carta / pasted), so it was not\n> mechanically verified against a structured source. Confirm each holder and class against\n> whatever these figures came from \u2014 the source document if there was one, or your own\n> share records if you described the cap table in conversation \u2014 before relying on them.\n\n## Current Cap State\n\nAs of: 2026-10-24\n\n| Holder | Shares (as-converted) | % of FD |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Alex Stone | 4,000,000 | 44.4% |\n| Sam Lee | 3,500,000 | 38.9% |\n| Options outstanding | 500,000 | 5.6% |\n| Options available | 1,000,000 | 11.1% |\n| **Total fully-diluted** | **9,000,000** | **100.0%** |\n\nOutstanding SAFEs: 1\n\n## Scenarios Modeled\n\n### Cap-implied SAFE snapshot (pre-financing) (SAFE conversion)\n\n**Stage:** Structure only \u2014 no priced round yet (`structural_only`)\n_Cap-implied: the ownership each SAFE locks in from its valuation cap, before a priced round sets the actual share price._\n\n**Cap-implied ownership (pre-financing):**\n- Foobar Capital LLC (`safe_foobar`): 5.0% cap-implied (SAFE price $1.0556, 473,684 shares)\n\n_Provenance: rules: `safe.stacked_post_money_caps`_\n\n### Series A at $16M pre / $4M raise (Priced round)\n\n**Stage:** Fully modeled (`full`)\n\n**Inputs:**\n- `pre_money`: 16000000\n- `new_money`: 4000000\n\n**Post-round ownership:**\n- founders pct: 63.3%\n- preferred pct: 0.0%\n- option pool pct: 12.7%\n- safe pct: 4.0%\n- note pct: 0.0%\n- new money pct: 20.0%\n- each founder, post-round:\n  - Alex Stone: 33.8% (4,000,000 shares)\n  - Sam Lee: 29.6% (3,500,000 shares)\n  - *(Founders only. Shares held through employee/other common batches are counted in the totals above but are not broken out per person here.)*\n\n**Equity financing price:** $1.6889/share\n\n**Founder Impact Lens:** Founders collectively held 83.3% of fully-diluted shares before this scenario; after, 63.3%. That's -20.0 percentage points.\n\n**Per-SAFE conversion math:**\n\n| SAFE | Branch | Purchase \u00f7 Cap | Conversion price | Conversion shares |\n|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n| Foobar Capital LLC (`safe_foobar`) | Cap and discount both applied \u2014 whichever gave more shares | \u2014 | $1.0556 | 473,684 |\n\n_Provenance: rules: `safe.post_money_cap_conversion`_\n\n## Scenario Comparison\n\n| Scenario | Stage | Founder %  | Equity Price |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n| Cap-implied SAFE snapshot (pre-financing) | Structure only \u2014 no priced round yet | \u2014 | \u2014 |\n| Series A at $16M pre / $4M raise | Fully modeled | 63.3% | $1.6889 |\n\n## Counsel Review Required\n\n### Delaware Cross Border\n- **[QSBS rules are date-sensitive](https://www.thetaxadviser.com/issues/2025/dec/revisiting-sec-1202-strategic-planning-after-the-2025-obbba-expansion/)** (`delaware_cross_border.qsbs_date_sensitive`)\n  - US QSBS eligibility and exclusion amounts are date-sensitive and changed for stock issued after July 4, 2025 under OBBBA; cap-table scripts should flag issue date and tax counsel review.\n\n## Date-Sensitive Watchlist\n\n_1 rule(s) to watch (from 1 matched instances)._\n\n| Rule | Status | When | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [QSBS rules are date-sensitive](https://www.thetaxadviser.com/issues/2025/dec/revisiting-sec-1202-strategic-planning-after-the-2025-obbba-expansion/) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the stock issue date for this instance. |\n\n### For-Reference Annotations\n\n_13 item(s) \u2014 rules that don't apply to this engagement in its current state (different jurisdiction, no grants, etc.) but are tracked in case the engagement evolves. No action needed today._\n\n## Sources Cited\n\n- `TAXADVISER-QSBS-OBBBA`\n\n---\n\n## Coaching Commentary\n\n**Your ownership story across scenarios**\n\nTwo scenarios were modeled. The cap-implied SAFE snapshot (`safe_cap_implied`) is structure only \u2014 it shows what the SAFE terms imply about pricing before any priced round happens, but produces no post-financing ownership table because no new money has been raised yet. All ownership figures below come from the Series A scenario (`series_a`).\n\nIn the Series A at $16M pre-money / $4M raise, the founders' collective stake moves from **83.3% to 63.3%** \u2014 a drop of **20 percentage points**. That is the headline number to keep in mind as you negotiate terms.\n\n**What's driving the dilution**\n\nTwo forces account for the full 20pp:\n\n- **New investor money ($4M)** accounts for 20pp of dilution. This is the straightforward cost of the round: new shares issued to investors at the Series A price.\n- **SAFE conversion** adds another 4pp. The outstanding SAFE converts into preferred shares at the financing, and those conversion shares come from the same fully-diluted pool that determines everyone's percentage. The SAFE's cap sets the conversion price; a lower cap means more shares to the SAFE holder relative to new investors, which is more dilution for founders.\n\nTogether these two drivers account for the full 20pp move. There is no option pool top-up modeled in this scenario, so that is not a factor here.\n\n**The one counsel item \u2014 QSBS timing**\n\nOne question was flagged for your attorney: whether any shares qualify under the QSBS rules (IRC \u00a71202, as updated by OBBBA \u2014 see `TAXADVISER-QSBS-OBBBA`). This is a date-sensitive determination. The cap-table math can confirm share counts and issuance structure, but it cannot conclude that shares do or do not qualify \u2014 that turns on facts your attorney must verify (gross asset test at issuance, active-business test, holding period, and the post-OBBBA acquisition-date boundary). Bring your share issuance dates and the company's asset history to that conversation.\n\n**Timing dates to track down**\n\nThe timing watchlist shows 13 instruments or events with no recorded date. None triggered an in-window, near-end, or expired status \u2014 but that is because the dates are missing, not because everything is clear. Date-sensitive rules (QSBS holding period, any \u00a7102 holding period if this company later operates in Israel, and note maturity clocks) cannot run without those dates. Gather the issuance date for each outstanding instrument and bring them to your attorney when you discuss the QSBS question above.\n\n**What to do before signing**\n\nThere are no hard blockers on either scenario \u2014 both ran to completion. The practical checklist before you sign:\n\n1. Confirm the SAFE conversion price is what you expect. The 4pp SAFE dilution flows from the cap and the pre-financing share count; if either is different from what you negotiated, the conversion shares will be different too.\n2. Ask your attorney about QSBS. The shares issued in this round could be eligible for a significant capital-gains exclusion if the conditions are met \u2014 this is worth the conversation.\n3. Collect issuance dates for every instrument. The date questions are unresolved and some of them have real legal and tax consequences.\n\nNo flip scenarios were modeled, and there is no divergence between any document-stated figure and the skill's computed math to flag.\n\n---\n\n*Generated by [founder skills](https://github.com/lool-ventures/founder-skills) by [lool ventures](https://lool.vc) \u2014 Cap Table Agent \u00b7 [Share feedback](https://github.com/lool-ventures/founder-skills/discussions/new?category=ideas-feedback)*\n",
